WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.731
So what makes anxiety healthy?

00:00:01.731 --> 00:00:05.433
Anxiety is healthy when it is 
serving as an alarm system

00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:07.519
that lets us know that something's not right,

00:00:07.519 --> 00:00:10.709
that it gets our&nbsp;attention and 
helps us to keep ourselves safe.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:15.571
The only time we consider anxiety to 
cross the line&nbsp;from healthy to unhealthy

00:00:15.571 --> 00:00:17.789
is under two conditions, actually.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.784
One is when we have anxiety, 
but there’s&nbsp;no threat,

00:00:20.784 --> 00:00:21.805
that there's nothing wrong.

00:00:21.805 --> 00:00:25.160
So if it's, you know, a lovely Sunday 
morning and you're&nbsp;taking a drive

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.827
and there's no traffic nearby,

00:00:26.827 --> 00:00:30.221
you shouldn't be having an 
anxiety response in&nbsp;that moment.

00:00:30.221 --> 00:00:33.822
And if you do, we would consider 
that grounds for concern.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:39.080
The other time we&nbsp;pay attention to 
anxiety and consider it to be unhealthy

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.772
is if the anxiety response is way&nbsp;
too big for what's happened,

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:44.728
out of proportion to events.

00:00:44.728 --> 00:00:48.278
So if somebody swerves and cut you off&nbsp;
and you have a panic attack in that moment,

00:00:48.278 --> 00:00:50.580
that is not healthy anxiety, 
it is not helping you.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.157
And&nbsp;we would address that clinically.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:57.097
Other than that, we really see anxiety 
as largely normal,&nbsp;protective, healthy

00:00:57.097 --> 00:00:59.080
and useful in our lives.

